 ### NeRF Pre-training (Density and Color)
-#### definition
-- [S5] Training the density net $\Theta_\sigma$ and color branch $\Theta_c$ using posed RGB images and an appearance loss, orthogonal to the Instance Field component.
-#### formula
-- [S5] Appearance loss: $L_p = \frac{1}{2|R|} \sum_{r \in R} \| \hat{C}(r) - C(r) \|^2$, where $R$ are sampled rays in a training batch, $C(r)$ is ground truth RGB, and $\hat{C}(r)$ is predicted RGB.
-#### parameter
-- [S5] $\Theta_\sigma$: Density network parameters.
-- [S5] $\Theta_c$: Color branch network parameters.
+- **Definition:** Training the density net $\Theta_\sigma$ and color branch $\Theta_c$ using posed RGB images and an appearance loss, orthogonal to the Instance Field component [S5].
